  "title": "Australia's Social Media Ban Legal Challenge Begins in High Court",
  "summary": "A rights group argues the Australian government's decision to pass a ban on social media access for under-16s is a legal loophole that limits free expression, while a high court challenges the policy as it proceeds.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Australian government passed a ban on social media access for under-16s in 2024, which led to legal disputes in the past.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A rights group challenges the ban, arguing it violates the right to free speech and political communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The ban was narrowed after Reddit sued the government, with the high court addressing the legal implications.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
